 "_note": "The one measurement plan_paper3 recommends before the third-paper decision, doing two jobs: testing whether F86's anchor survives a SECOND behavioural target (nucleus sampling -- a different decoder, and the one introduced to fix greedy degeneration), and re-testing F92's deflationary dissociation, where `modal` survived at rho=+0.60 p=0.13 and could still invert the reading. rep_stats/PROMPTS/NEW_TOKENS imported from degeneration_vs_tstar so the new targets sit on the old axis; bh_fdr imported. Every predictor is compared on the SAME rows. A sign flip on the primary makes branch B automatic, which was registered before the data existed."
